WebGL: recognize AGX renderer string in SanitizeRenderer

Mesa's 00-asahi-defaults.conf overrides GL_RENDERER to "AGX G13/G14" for web
browsers so Linux Apple Silicon users are not flagged by anti-bot checks that
reject "Apple" in the WebGL renderer string on non-macOS platforms
(webcompat/web-bugs#189524).

Firefox's ChooseDeviceReplacement() recognizes "Apple" and "llvmpipe" but not
"AGX", logging four GraphicsCriticalError crash annotations on every WebGL
page ("Couldn't sanitize GL_RENDERER \"AGX G13/G14\"") and falling back to
"Generic Renderer". Recognize the "AGX" prefix and replace it with "AGX"
(keeping "Apple" out of the sanitized string).

--- a/dom/canvas/SanitizeRenderer.cpp	2026-11-25 01:28:57.939801843 +1100
+++ b/dom/canvas/SanitizeRenderer.cpp	2026-11-25 01:28:57.943056839 +1100
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
     const std::string& str) {
   if (str.starts_with("llvmpipe")) return "llvmpipe";
   if (str.starts_with("Apple")) return "Apple M1";
+  if (str.starts_with("AGX")) return "AGX";
 
   std::smatch m;
 
